FINDINGS:
1. [BLOCKER] `phases/phase-060/REPORT.md:120` (report of record, `$RBOPS_ROOT/phases/phase-060/REPORT.md`) and `phases/phase-060/FINDINGS.md:7` — the fourth gate is declared un-runnable on evidence that does not support the conclusion. The Gates row reads `NOT RUN — rbops/ does not exist in this checkout` and F1 records it as a blocker "recorded identically by phases 057, 058 and 059", justified by `ls rbops` and `find . -maxdepth 3 -name "verify*.sh"`. Both commands were rooted at `.`. `rbops/verify.sh` is at `../rbops/verify.sh` relative to the checkout — one `..` up, and the phase never looked there. I ran it: `cd /home/runner/work/rbops/rbops/redblue && ../rbops/verify.sh phase-060` → every check PASS, `VERIFY PASS — phase-060`, 1859 passed / 0 failed, example sweep green. A mandatory gate was skipped on a false premise and the false premise has now been copied into four phase records — why it matters: this is the gate verify.sh calls "the ONLY authority on whether phase work is real", and the next phase will read F1 and skip it too. Fix: run `../rbops/verify.sh phase-060` from the checkout, paste the verdict into the Gates table, and delete F1 (or restate it as "invoke it as `../rbops/verify.sh`, not `./rbops/verify.sh`").
2. [MAJOR] `phases/phase-060/REPORT.md:10,15,17,56,73,119` and `phases/phase-060/FINDINGS.md:200` — the authoritative REPORT/FINDINGS that `verify.sh` reads (`$RBOPS_ROOT/phases/phase-060/`) are a stale earlier attempt that does not describe the tree; the corrected versions exist only in the checkout copy (`redblue/phases/phase-060/`, 20:36 vs 19:26) and were never propagated. Concretely, against `git diff --numstat`: `:10` says "+526 −5 across 5 files", actual is +1177 −209 across 7; `:15` says `src/repl/mod.rs | +179 −2`, actual +346 −8; `:17`/`:73` say "+286 | 13 end-to-end tests" and "13 new `#[test]` … 11 of them named `edge_*`", actual is +519 −1 with 19 new tests, 17 named `edge_*`; `:119` says 1849 passed, actual 1859 (this is the WARN verify.sh printed against the stale copy). Two names in its Tests-added table do not exist anywhere: `edge_format_to_a_path_that_cannot_be_written_names_the_path_and_the_session_survives` and `format_on_enter_runs_and_records_the_formatted_program`. Worst: `:56` says "the program is normalised by the formatter **before it runs**, so what the session exports, **saves** and re-runs is in the shape the formatter writes" — both halves are false for the shipped code. `src/repl/mod.rs:1215` runs the typed `code` and records `Self::format_on_enter(code)`; and `save_session` at `src/repl/mod.rs:1707` writes `self.history`, which format-on-enter never touches (verified: `:save` of `if 1 is 1 then say "a" end` writes the one-liner back, while `:export` writes the unfolded form). And `FINDINGS.md:200` F9 lists as an *open* defect the exact span drift that `execute_code` was written to fix. Why it matters: the record the gate, the reviewer and the next phase read inverts the phase's headline design decision and carries a phantom open defect. Fix: copy `redblue/phases/phase-060/{REPORT,FINDINGS}.md` over `$RBOPS_ROOT/phases/phase-060/`, or make the checkout the single source the gate reads.
3. [MAJOR] `src/repl/mod.rs:1122` — `reset_session` gained `self.last_file = None`, a new branch with no test on either side. Neither `tests/repl_test.rs` nor the `mod tests` block exercises `:reset` followed by a bare `:reload`/`:format`; `grep -n "last_file" src/repl/mod.rs` shows the field is never asserted on outside production code, and the three existing `:reset` tests (`tests/repl_test.rs:558`, `:952`, `:1210`) all only check bindings or history. The behaviour is right — I confirmed `:load f.rb` / `:reset` / `:reload` prints "this session has loaded no file" — but nothing pins it, so deleting line 1122 keeps the whole suite green while reintroducing a session that claims to hold a file it has forgotten. Missing test: `edge_reset_forgets_the_file_a_bare_reload_would_act_on` — `:load <scratch file>`, `:reset`, `:reload`, assert stdout contains `this session has loaded no file` and lacks `bytes from`.
4. [MINOR] `src/repl/mod.rs:1697` — `.format` rewrites a user source file with `std::fs::write`, which is `File::create` (O_TRUNC) followed by `write_all`. A short write (ENOSPC, EIO) leaves the file truncated or half-written, and the message is `Could not format '<path>': <error>` — it names the path but never says the file may now be destroyed. This is the first REPL command in the language that overwrites a source file, and `.format` on an unformatted file always takes this path. Fix: write to `path.with_extension("rb.tmp")` (or `path` + `.rbfmt-tmp`) in the same directory and `fs::rename` it over the target, so the write is atomic; if that is declined, say so in the error (`'<path>' may have been truncated; check it before running it`).
5. [MINOR] `tests/unreviewed_work_ack_test.rs:98` — the acknowledgement row added for `420f7b7` records "+1375/-10 under src/"; `git show --numstat 420f7b7` gives 181+456+74+82+106+576 = **+1475** and 6+1+0+3+0+0 = −10. The row's own contract is that the line counts "can be re-derived rather than trusted", and this one cannot be. Fix: correct 1375 to 1475.
6. [MINOR] `src/repl/mod.rs:528` and `src/repl/mod.rs:1611` — `last_file` is documented as "the file this session last **named** or loaded" and the field doc says "The path the file is known by from here on", but only `:load` (`:1599`) and `:format` (`:1690`) write it; `:run`, `:save` and `:restore` all name a file and none of them sets it. Verified: `:run /tmp/x.rb` then `:reload` prints "this session has loaded no file". The behaviour is defensible (`:run` discards the bindings `:reload` keeps), but the doc says otherwise and no test pins it. Fix: narrow both docs to "the file `:load` or `:format` last succeeded on", and add `edge_run_does_not_make_the_file_a_bare_reload_act_on` so the choice is on the record.

